   ],
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Sound effects from a text prompt (Stable Audio Open 1.0)\n\n**The SFX flow.** Every other audio model here makes *music*; this one was trained for **sound effects and\nfield recordings** - 486,492 CC-licensed clips from Freesound and the Free Music Archive - and Stability's own\nmodel card says it is *better at those than at music*, naming footsteps, door creaks and environmental sounds\nfor games. So this is where a footstep/impact/ambience palette comes from.\n\nIt is also the cheapest model in the scenario to run: one **4.5 GB** checkpoint (the text encoder is inside it)\nin `models/checkpoints/`, and no custom nodes - the graph is core ComfyUI only.\n\n- **the text encoder is a separate download.** The checkpoint carries no CLIP, so `t5-base.safetensors` goes in\n  `models/text_encoders/` and the `CLIPLoader` has `type: stable_audio`. Running it without that fails with\n  *\"clip input is invalid\"* - the error names the cause if you read it.\n\n- **the prompt is the effect**, and it wants to be concrete: *\"footsteps on gravel\"*, *\"a heavy wooden door\n  creaking\"*, *\"a sword drawn from a scabbard\"*. Not a scene description.\n- **`FloatConstant` is the length** and feeds both `ConditioningStableAudio.seconds_total` and\n  `EmptyLatentAudio.seconds` - the conditioning and the latent must agree. Up to ~47 s.\n- **50 steps / cfg 7 / `dpmpp_3m_sde` / `karras`** is the reference sampler setting for this model; shorter\n  lengths let you raise the batch and get a set in one run.\n- **Its limits, from its own card:** no realistic vocals, English-only descriptions, and music is its weak\n  case (for music use `ace-step.json`).\n\n*How to run it: story S21 in `HOWTO.md`  ·  Why it is this way: E11 in `audio/EXPERIMENTS.md`.*\n"
   ],
